From b5507f124c8234cebd9558ed6c042413f67dc990 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:50:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the character reference mandatory, and scoped
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two defects on the same chain, found together.

First: a provider that cannot read reference images accepted these calls
anyway. `replicate` has supportsImageInput:false, so every character
keyframe was generated from prompt text alone with the approved reference
silently discarded — a new face and a new costume in every scene, and
nothing in the result to say the anchor had been dropped. Guided Story
never had this because its cast-frame call passes requireReferenceInput;
the character path passed nothing. Both character call sites now pass it,
so an incapable pin reroutes to a capable provider or refuses, instead of
degrading into confident nonsense.

Second, which only became visible once the first was fixed: with the
reference finally being consumed, the reference's own background came
with it. Outfit references are deliberately shot against a neutral studio
wall (outfitVariantPrompt asks for exactly that), and sceneKeyframePrompt
never said not to copy it — so a hospital scene rendered as a grey
seamless. The prompt now scopes the reference to identity and clothing
only, and takes background, pose, camera angle and framing from the scene
direction, naming the studio backdrop as the thing to exclude.

The existing assertion on "authoritative for both identity and clothing"
is updated rather than kept: that phrasing is the bug.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fm1CGTe9kKKt48ZPVyQMh1
